![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `sortValue` function uses `localeCompare` without a specified locale. This can lead to non-deterministic sorting and hash mismatches across different system environments with different default locales. It is highly recommended to use a simple, locale-independent comparison to ensure cryptographic consistency.

```javascript
export function sortValue(value) {
  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.map(sortValue);
  if (value && typeof value === 'object') {
    return Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(value).sort(([left], [right]) => {
      if (left < right) return -1;
      if (left > right) return 1;
      return 0;
    }).map(([key, item]) => [key, sortValue(item)]));
  }
  return value;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Avoid using Intl.Collator with an undefined locale for sorting, as it can introduce locale-sensitive discrepancies across different runtime environments. Instead, use a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison to ensure locale-independent, deterministic ordering.
</details>

