![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

In `boundedQuestionRows`, if the `following` question label is found on an earlier page of `page_chain`, the code slices `selected` but continues the loop for subsequent pages, appending all their rows to `bounded`. This results in incorrect transcriptions. Breaking the loop once the boundary is found ensures that subsequent pages are not incorrectly appended.

```javascript
    const following = question.following_question_label;
    if (following) {
      const boundary = selected.findIndex((row) => row.minX < 65
        && new RegExp(`^\\s*${following}(?:\\s+\\S|\\s*$)`).test(row.text));
      if (boundary >= 0) {
        selected = selected.slice(0, boundary);
        bounded.push(...selected.map((row) => ({ ...row, page_number: pageNumber })));
        break;
      } else if (pageNumber === question.following_question_page) {
        throw new Error('printed question boundary end was not found');
      }
    }
    bounded.push(...selected.map((row) => ({ ...row, page_number: pageNumber })));
```

